{%- comment -%}
  PG Gift Pill: the FREE GIFT badge sits under the product title, hugging its
  own words. Two inline declarations pg-drawer writes are the reason it never
  did, and neither can be beaten from a stylesheet.

  pg-drawer's giftTag() stamps the pill with a list of INLINE !important styles
  the moment it is created, and ftFix() then re-pins two of them on its own
  schedule. Inline !important outranks every stylesheet rule, including rules at
  four ids, so the CSS written for this pill in pg-cart-tune was never applied.
  Measured, at 390px, against the drawer's real geometry:

      display was inline-flex  ->  the pill rode along on the TITLE'S OWN LINE,
                                   its box starting 170px to the right of the R
      width:auto (this file's
      earlier fix)             ->  a display:flex box inside the block-level h2
                                   fills the h2's whole width: a full-width
                                   purple bar, which is the "purple extending
                                   too far to the left"

  So both are set in script, where they can actually win:

      display: flex          the pill takes the line under the title
      width:  fit-content    it hugs its words instead of filling the line

  Measured after: on its own line, pill.left - title.left = 0px, 85px of pill
  for 63px of text -- 11px of padding a side and nothing more.

  AND THEN THE WORDS. Aligning the BOX was not the ask. Measured off the owner's
  screenshot at 390pt: the title's glyphs start at 148.2px and the pill's box at
  148.2px -- but its WORDS start at 162.1px, because the box carries 11px of
  padding and a rounded cap. "Move the text over left more to be under the R36S"
  is about the words, and they were 14px right of the R.

  So the pill is pulled left by exactly its own left padding. The glyphs then
  begin on the title's own left edge, and the purple overhangs by those 11px --
  into the row's padding, where there is room, and small enough not to read as
  the wide bar the earlier width:auto bug produced.

  WHY ITS OWN FILE. pg-cart-tune already owns this pill's placement and would be
  the natural home, but that file is 28KB and every edit to it means re-sending
  the whole thing. This is four property writes on one element. It runs AFTER
  pg-cart-tune's own pass in the same section group, so where the two agree the
  second write is a no-op, and where they differ this one is the later word.

  It cannot fight ftFix: ftFix only re-pins `width` and `text-indent`, both of
  which this re-asserts on the same clock, and each write is guarded on the
  value already there, so a settled pill is never touched.
{%- endcomment -%}
<script>
(function(){
  if (window.pgGiftPill) return; window.pgGiftPill = 1;

  function fit(){
    document.querySelectorAll('#cart .pg-free-tag, body.template-cart .pg-free-tag').forEach(function(tag){
      var li = tag.closest('li');
      var h2 = li && li.querySelector('h2');
      if (h2 && tag.parentNode !== h2) h2.appendChild(tag);

      if (tag.style.display !== 'flex'){
        tag.style.setProperty('display', 'flex', 'important');
        tag.style.setProperty('justify-content', 'flex-start', 'important');
        tag.style.setProperty('align-items', 'center', 'important');
        tag.style.setProperty('text-align', 'left', 'important');
        tag.style.setProperty('padding', '6px 11px', 'important');
        /* -11px == the left padding, so the WORDS start on the title's left
           edge rather than the box doing so. See the note above. */
        tag.style.setProperty('margin', '5px 0 1px -11px', 'important');
      }
      if (tag.style.width !== 'fit-content'){
        tag.style.setProperty('width', '-webkit-fit-content', 'important');
        tag.style.setProperty('width', 'fit-content', 'important');
      }
      if (tag.style.textIndent !== '0px') tag.style.setProperty('text-indent', '0', 'important');
    });
  }

  var pending = false;
  function soon(){
    if (pending) return;
    pending = true;
    setTimeout(function(){ pending = false; fit(); }, 80);
  }

  if (window.MutationObserver){
    (function watch(){
      var c = document.getElementById('cart');
      if (c){ try { new MutationObserver(soon).observe(c, {childList:true, subtree:true}); } catch(e){} }
      else setTimeout(watch, 500);
    })();
  }
  /* ftFix runs at creation and again at 400/1500/3500ms and on fonts.ready,
     then stops; these land just after each of its passes */
  [450, 1550, 3550, 4200].forEach(function(ms){ setTimeout(fit, ms); });
  setInterval(fit, 1200);
  fit();
})();
</script>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Gift Pill", "settings": []}
{% endschema %}
